From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: MPEG-4 Part 2 decoding (not upstream uAPI)

The video engine's MPEG engine decodes MPEG-4 Part 2 (Simple and
Advanced Simple Profile), which mainline has no stateless API for. Add,
not upstream:

- V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_VOP ('MG4V'): one VOP per OUTPUT buffer;
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_VOP: a U8 array holding struct
  v4l2_ctrl_mpeg4_vop, the parsed VOL/VOP header fields, the bit offset
  of the first macroblock, the B-VOP TRB/TRD and the references.

and cedrus_mpeg4.c, programming the engine as libvdpau-sunxi does
(VOPHDR 0x04, TRBTRD 0x20/0x24, the MBH/DCAC/NCF work buffers at
0x38/0x3c/0x44, QP 0x84, MPEG-4 trigger over all macroblocks), with the
MPEG quantisation matrices loaded as MPEG-2's. Enabled on suniv.

As libvdpau-sunxi: VOPs without resync markers only, no S(GMC)-VOPs,
and no H.263 short header or Sorenson Spark (the engine's switch for
those is not known).
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ioctl.c
@@ -1510,6 +1510,7 @@
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_ANNEX_L:	descr = "VC-1 (SMPTE 412M Annex L)"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP8:		descr = "VP8"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP8_FRAME:    descr = "VP8 Frame"; break;
+		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_VOP:	descr = "MPEG-4 Part 2 Parsed VOP"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9:		descr = "VP9"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME:    descr = "VP9 Frame"; break;
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC:		descr = "HEVC"; break; /* aka H.265 */
